; tap2sna.py file for Knight Lore. Run
;
;   $ tap2sna.py @knightlore.t2s
;
; to create a Z80 snapshot.

https://zxaaa.net/DENIED/Knight%20Lore%20(1984)(Ultimate%20Play%20The%20Game).tzx
KnightLore.z80

--sim-load-config accelerator=speedlock

; The Speedlock loader decrypts its second stage (at $F230) from the BASIC
; program, then loads the loading screen at $4000 and the game at $6100. Its
; final stub (LD A,($F225); CP $00; JP NZ,$0000; LD SP,$60FE; LD IY,$5C3A;
; JP $6100) hands over to the game, so stopping the simulation at the game's
; entry point ($6100: DI; LD SP,$5BA0; JP $AF6C) leaves the snapshot with
; everything at the real addresses and the loading screen intact.
--start 24832
--stack 23456

; The game uses $5B00-$60FF (the printer buffer, the system variables and the
; BASIC program that the loader left behind) as its own variable area and
; clears it itself, so start with it empty. The same goes for the screen
; buffer and the lookup tables above the game ($D900-$FFFF), which the game
; builds at run-time; this also removes what the loader left at $F230.
--ram poke=$5B00-$60FF,$00
--ram poke=$D900-$FFFF,$00
